.llossless-cache/
__pycache__/
.venv/
*.pyc
.env
/internal/assets/

# Run output written into the repo root: -o merges and piped reports. These
# carry the source documents' content, which is the same content /internal/assets/ is
# ignored for, and they are named by whoever ran the command -- so they are
# matched by position rather than by name. Ignoring a path does nothing to a
# tracked one, so README.md, STATE.md, CHANGELOG.md, MEMORY.md, HISTORY.md and
# publication-manifest.txt keep showing their edits; only new root files are
# swallowed. A root file that genuinely belongs in the repo goes in with
# `git add -f`, or lives in docs/ like every other document here.
/*.md
/*.txt

# internal/TODO.md is TRACKED. It was ignored here once, on the reasoning
# that it is a working note rather than a result (332) -- which was true and
# was also an argument for HISTORY.md and MEMORY.md, both tracked below.
# 332 is superseded (344): DA's freeze parks findings in this file, and an
# untracked file is absent from the object store, from the CO item 0b mirror,
# and from any clone. It is withheld from publication by living in internal/,
# which is the whole mechanism -- not by being hidden from Git.

# HISTORY.md and MEMORY.md are TRACKED. They were ignored here once, and the
# patterns came out when the decision changed; this comment survived them and
# said the opposite of the truth until 2026-08-23. They are working records, so
# they are withheld from publication instead, by name, in
# publication-manifest.txt. Git tracking and publication are separate decisions
# and this file only makes the first one.


# The role -> model id map. Untracked because it is one machine's configuration,
# not because a model id is secret; models.local.example.json shows the shape.
models.local.json

# Exploratory cross-model cassettes. Recorded from a dirty tree and against
# prompts that no longer exist, so no commit reproduces them and no current run
# can hit their keys. tests/eval/README.md is tracked and explains them; the
# cassettes are not.
tests/eval/*/

# What the last finished run of `tests/run_all.py` proved, and about which
# tree. Read by `scripts/hooks/pre-commit`. Untracked because it is a fact
# about one working copy at one moment: committing it would publish a claim
# that the next person to clone has no way to have earned (299).
/.suite-stamp.json
